sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-11> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because Anthrobot movement types are highly consistent and rarely interconvert (for example between circular and linear), the authors conclude that Anthrobots self-organize into discrete, stable movement types, each bot having a distinct motility fingerprint.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Anthrobots self-organize into discrete, stable movement types with individual fingerprints";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Gumuskaya G, Srivastava P, Cooper BG, Lesser H, Semegran B, Garnier S, Levin M, “Motile Living Biobots Self-Construct from Adult Human Somatic Progenitor Seed Cells”, Advanced science (Weinheim, Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany) (2024), doi:10.1002/advs.202303575; section “Results › Anthrobots Self‐Organize into Discrete Movement Types”. Scope: NHBE-derived Anthrobots in vitro"
}
